/**
@page architecture Telematics SDK Classes

This section describes the hierarchy for the public classes.

The following diagram shows the relationship between the major components involved
in building the Telematics SDK.

@anchor fig_class_diagram
@latexonly
\begin{figure}[H]
  \centering
  \includegraphics[scale=0.08]{../../images/class_diagram.png}
  \renewcommand{\thefigure}{\thechapter-\arabic{figure}}
  \caption{SDK-Classdiagram}
  \label{fig_class_diagram}
\end{figure}
@endlatexonly

@html_image{class_diagram.png,SDK-Classdiagram,20,20,SDK-Classdiagram}

Telematics SDK can be broadly divided into the following types of modules:

- Manager - A set of manager classes such as PhoneManager, CallManager, SMSManager, CardManager etc.
- Observer/ Listener - Listener for unsolicited response messages coming out of RIL layer.
- Services (Call, SMS, CardServices) - APIs for Telematics functions.
- Logger - APIs to log messages, control the log levels.

Telematics SDK implements following classes:
- PhoneFactory - PhoneFactory is the central factory to create Telematics SDK Classes and services.
- IPhoneManager - PhoneManager is one of the main classes for Telephony applications. It is responsible for initialization of the telephony subsystem, enumerate phones and provides interface for registering listeners.
- IPhoneListener - A listener class for monitoring changes in specific telephony states on the device, including call state change, incoming SMS, incoming voice call etc.
- IPhone - This class allows making phone calls, getting system information and registering for system events. Each Phone instance is associated with a single SIM slot.
- SignalStrength - Contains phone signal strength related information.
- ICall - This class is the primary interface to perform call related operations including hold, hangup etc. It represents a call in progress. An ICall cannot be directly created by the user, rather it is returned as a result of instantiating a call, or from the PhoneListener.
- ICallManager -  Call Manager does aggregate state management for in progress calls.
- ISmsManager - SMS Manager class is the primary interface to send and receive SMS messages. It allows to send an SMS in several formats and sizes.
- SmsMessage - A Short Message Service message.
- ICardManager - ICardManager provides the interface for all SIM Card services.
- ICard - Represents a single card.
- ICardApp - Represents a single card application on a SIM Card.

*/
